<title>TURKEY: Turkish stocks fall sharply on high rates.</title>
<headline>Turkish stocks fall sharply on high rates.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish stocks fell sharply in thin trade dominated by high interest rates and liquidity shortage in money and bond markets, brokers said.</p>
<p>The IMKB National-100 closed at  1,836 on Monday, down 53 points, or 2.81 percent from Friday's close.</p>
